    "final_answer": "I have verified my findings. Let me summarize the results:\n\n## Three Most Popular Newly Released Open-Source NLP Translation Models on Hugging Face\n\nI navigated to Hugging Face's Models page, filtered by the **Translation** pipeline tag, and sorted by **Recently Created**. Based on download counts (the primary popularity indicator for new models), here are the three most popular new translation models:\n\n### 1. **pek01/rillio-subtitle-pack**\n- **Downloads last month:** 337\n- **Updated:** ~1 day ago\n- **License:** Apache-2.0 (open-source)\n- **Pipeline:** Translation\n- **Parameters:** 2B\n- **URL:** https://huggingface.co/pek01/rillio-subtitle-pack\n\n### 2. **mradermacher/ChindaMT-4B-GGUF**\n- **Downloads last month:** 308\n- **Updated:** ~3 days ago\n- **License:** Apache-2.0 (open-source)\n- **Pipeline:** Translation\n- **Parameters:** 5B (GGUF quantized format)\n- **Base model:** Qwen3.5-4B-Base finetuned to iapp/ChindaMT-4B\n- **URL:** https://huggingface.co/mradermacher/ChindaMT-4B-GGUF\n\n### 3. **Arushhh/indic-translate-mar-bhili-lora**\n- **Downloads last month:** 200\n- **Updated:** ~3 days ago\n- **License:** indic-open-model-license-v1.0 (open-source)\n- **Pipeline:** Translation\n- **Type:** PEFT LoRA adapter for Marathi ↔ Dehwali Bhili translation\n- **Base model:** google/gemma-4-E4B (via bodhan-ai/indic-translate)\n- **URL:** https://huggingface.co/Arushhh/indic-translate-mar-bhili-lora\n\nAll three models were created within the past 3 days (well within the past month), have open-source licenses, and are tagged as Translation NLP models.",
